From: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/panel: himax-hx83121a: report a linear backlight scale

The 12-bit brightness register is linear in panel luminance from at least
level 256 up. Say so: userspace otherwise applies a perceptual curve of its
own on top, as drm_hwcomposer does for an unknown or non-linear scale.
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-himax-hx83121a.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-himax-hx83121a.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-himax-hx83121a.c
index 15bbc1f91..f25a37881 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-himax-hx83121a.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-himax-hx83121a.c
@@ -214,7 +214,7 @@ himax_create_backlight(struct mipi_dsi_device *dsi)
 		.type = BACKLIGHT_RAW,
 		.brightness = 512,
 		.max_brightness = 4095,
-		.scale = BACKLIGHT_SCALE_NON_LINEAR,
+		.scale = BACKLIGHT_SCALE_LINEAR,
 	};
 
 	return devm_backlight_device_register(dev, dev_name(dev), dev, dsi,
